  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Road Management and Rural Roads Improvement Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project will comprise the following components, detailed descriptions of which are presented 
in Appendix 2.2.
(a) Infrastructure Works:
(i) Rehabilitation of approximately 5 km of existing village/feeder roads;
(ii) Routine maintenance activities; and
(iii) Labour-based maintenance works on selected roads.
(b) Engineering and Construction-related Services: Consulting services for the design and construction supervision of the rehabilitation works. Draft Terms of Reference (TOR) for 
the services are presented at Appendix 2.3.
(c) Goods:
(i) Computer equipment for operation of a RAMS;
(ii) Data collection equipment for a RAMS; and
(iii) Equipment and spare parts for road maintenance by BRAGSA.
(d) Institutional Strengthening: Consulting services to develop a RAMS for the road network in SVG; provide recommendations for financing road maintenance, including in respect of amendments to legislation or regulations; and to strengthen the capacity of MTW and BRAGSA to undertake hazard and climate vulnerability and risk assessments of critical infrastructure. The draft TOR is presented at Appendix 2.4- 4 -
(e) Capacity Building: Consulting services to provide training in labour-based maintenance to BRAGSA and MTW staff, small contractors and community-based groups. The draft TOR is presented at Appendix 2.5. 
(f) Project Management: Services including:
(i) Consulting services for GOSVG Coordinator and GOSVG Engineer. Draft TORs 
are shown at Appendices 2.6 and 2.7, respectively.
(ii) Services by CDB and GOSVG staff to manage implementation, including a 
Community Liaison Officer (CLO) assigned by MTW (duties detailed at Appendix 2.8) and a Project Liaison Officer assigned by BRAGSA; and (iii) Consulting and non-consulting services for implementation of communication and visibility requirements (see TOR at Appendix 2.9).</narrative>
  </description>
